# Phase 18 P18-V01 `MqClientAdmin.getConsumerConnectionList` — 2026-10-18T04:59:56Z

## Scope and implementation

- Continued on `phase/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate`. The pinned Java
  5.5.1 oracle at `/Users/bruce.tsai/Projects/3rd/rocketmq` remained read-only.
  Existing Phase 19 worktree changes were not staged or modified.
- Added `MQClientApi::get_consumer_connection_list` and the
  `MqClientAdmin` adapter for asynchronous request code 203. Added typed
  `Connection` and `ConsumerConnection` response DTOs with Java-compatible
  enum names, nullable collection/body behavior, and `SubscriptionData`
  decoding.
- Added the `GetConsumerConnectionListRequestHeader` and the previously
  started `GetConsumeStatsRequestHeader` to Java/Rust header inventory,
  identity, validation, and bidirectional wire fixtures. The consume-stats
  helper methods are checked against the generated Java header fixture.
- Extended `MqClientAdminFixtures` with success, null body, and Broker-error
  outcomes; the response contains one connection and a populated subscription.
  Core scripted coverage compares request fields and decoded result, and rejects
  malformed success bodies. Fixture SHA-256:
  `63fedb0e501c7539fcbf9495a639c41ec59aa8e3e8db39a14a75674c1a1f2a05`.
- Code commit: `eb627fcc` (`feat(admin): match consumer connection list adapter`).
  Updated the Phase 17 admin matrix, `REQUEST_CODES.md`, and release checklist.

